<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23899" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-somnis</span></b> , e, adj.
		2. in-somnus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>sleepless</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in
			post-Aug. prose). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Of
			living beings, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3, 7, 8</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juventus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					3, 54</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insomnes magis, quam pervigiles,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					1, 65</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">draco,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					9, 190</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Of
			things: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oculi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 3, 328</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dens,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of the dragon</i>, <i>from which armed men
						sprung</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					4, 552</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nox,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 9, 167</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					2, 239</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
